type mismatch:

Assumption: Coral.Frame.nrows takes a Frame, not a scalar. Passing an i64
must be rejected during checking with a Frame-vs-i64 type mismatch (the pinned
fragment stays mangle-insensitive: upstream demangles user-facing renderings
over time, e.g. chelis#399, and the case is narrow enough that any type
mismatch here is the intended rejection). If the
checker ever accepts this program, the negative suite should report an
unexpected pass rather than silently coercing the scalar.
